DESCRIPTION:Topic: The Playability Gap: Measuring the Child-Friendliness o
 f Urban Neighbourhoods\n\nHow well do urban neighbourhoods support young c
 hildren's outdoor free play — and why does it matter? Dr. Emily Gemmell 
 discusses the development of an urban playability index for young children
 \, how neighbourhood-level scores vary across Canada's 35 largest cities a
 nd what this means for children's health and development.\n\nSpeakers: Emi
 ly Gemmell\n\nEmily is a post-doctoral environmental health researcher at 
 the University of British Columbia. Her work focuses on how urban environm
 ents impact health across the lifespan.\n\nAgenda:\n\n7:00-7:20 Welcome an
 d Introductions\n\n7:20-7:50 Presentation and Q\\&A/discussion\n\n7:50-9:0
 0 Breakout groups\n\nCode of Conduct:\n\nhttps://civictech.ca/about-us\n\n
